0..76 Comment "// A recursive call at a variable converts through the arm that waits on it."
77..151 Comment "// `wind(Loop(x))` runs to the `Loop` arm, whose `run` waits on `wind(x)`,"
152..230 Comment "// stuck at the variable; an endpoint\'s computation is pure, so the bind reads"
231..307 Comment "// as the arm\'s constructor over the held call, `S(wind(x))`, and the kernel"
308..385 Comment "// replays the reading by forcing it. An arm that cases on the call before it"
386..464 Comment "// returns keeps the call stuck, and a path stating a value for it is refused."
